WEBVTT

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:23.860
<i>Everyday I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:31.200
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:38.930
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.010
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:49.780
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:57.560
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:04.530
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:12.460
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:20.140
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:33.690
"Traffic Department"

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:36.660
lmpostor #704?!

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.090
Isn't that the thief who
wears a disguise...

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.640
...and preys on older people
who live alone?

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.100
That's right.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.230
Any recent robberies
in this area...

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.570
...could be the work
of lmpostor #704.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.000
I see.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:55.950
So that's why we've been
called in to help.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:57.850
Well, you can count
on me!

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:01.910
I'll catch that rotten
thief for you, Chief!

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:04.710
Hang on, Tsujimoto. That's
not what I had in mind.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:09.920
Actually, I want each of you to pay
a visit on some older folks.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.260
Visit?

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:14.520
You're always jumping to
conclusions, Natsumi.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.790
I want you to gain
their trust...

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:21.310
...so they'll be sure to call us
if anything happens to them.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:23.770
Yes, sir!

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:28.850
FILE. 2B
CHASE DOWN
IMPOSTOR NO. 704!

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:34.480
Let me see...

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:37.520
Mr. Genzo Yamada,
78 years old.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:41.080
He lived with his son's family
up until last year.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.090
His wife passed away
three years ago.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.560
Oh, my. So he suddenly had
to face life all by himself.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.100
How lonely.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.230
Yeah. Anyway, let's
say hello to him.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:53.670
Yes?

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:54.870
Hello!

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:55.970
What is it?

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.700
Are you Mr. Genzo
Yamada?

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.480
Who are you?

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.340
We're from Bokuto Station.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.140
We've come to speak
with you today.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:06.810
Y... You're...

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.580
...Kinuko!

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:12.620
Wait! She's not Kinuko,
sir. She's Aoi Futaba.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:15.690
And I'm Yoriko Nikaidou.
Nice to meet you...

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:15.930
Tomie!

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:17.420
No! No, wait!

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.560
Hello!

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.100
Yes? Who is it?

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:34.210
Umm, hello! Are you
Ms. Sayuri Tanaka?

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:36.110
Who are you?

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:40.350
Umm... I'm Nakajima, from
Bokuto Station.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.990
My, aren't you
diligent?

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.550
Well, it's nothing.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.220
Mr. Mailman?

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:49.950
Huh? No, no, ma'am.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.600
I'm a police
officer.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:53.750
Is that so?

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:55.760
I've come to speak
with you today...

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:57.890
...and I was wondering...

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.990
...if you're free now?

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.370
Wait a second.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.270
Yes?

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.500
You're not the
mailman?

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:10.050
No, like I said, I'm
a police officer.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:15.020
Well, isn't that something? I was
certain you were a mailman.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.850
Isn't this
lovely...

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:25.020
...having a handsome young man
come just to speak with me.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.690
Thank you for making time for me,
ma'am, sorry to be a bother.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.490
Now don't you say another
word about it.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:34.270
The pleasure's all mine. Here,
have a seat. Please.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.840
Uh, thank you.

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:38.740
I'll just go put
on some tea.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.570
You wait right there.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:43.210
Don't go out of your
way for me!

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.980
Hmm. Ms. Sayuri Tanaka,
79 years old.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.880
Her husband died
in the war...

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:53.820
...and her family all died in the
fire raids, during the war.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.720
She sure has had
a tough life.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:58.490
I better be extra
sensitive here.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.900
So I look like your wife, when
she was a young woman?

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:08.060
And I look like your
first sweetheart?

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:09.570
Mmm-hmm.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:12.670
They've both passed away...

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:15.580
So when I saw you at the door, I was sure
they'd come to lead me to the next world!

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.580
It's too early
for that!

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.880
That's right, you've still got
lots of years ahead of you!

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.810
Think so?

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.050
Sure! You have to
think positively!

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:25.880
You're still
young!

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:27.990
Hearing you talk
that way...

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:30.220
...makes me feel
a lot better.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.130
That's the spirit!

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:43.700
Sure is taking her a long time to make
tea. It's been 15 minutes...

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:47.970
Wait a sec. Maybe some-
thing's happened.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:54.510
Ms. Tanaka?

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:56.750
She's not here.

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:59.620
That's strange.

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:00.520
Huh?

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.620
That noise was coming
from the bath.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:09.520
Oh! Maybe it's
that thief!

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.000
I've got to save
Ms. Tanaka!

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:14.500
Ms. Tanaka!

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:18.180
Oh, no! You pervert!

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:23.240
"You pervert?" But,
Ms. Tanaka...

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:25.380
Excuse me, ma'am!
Forgive me!

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.220
What on earth?

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:30.720
My goodness.

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:33.720
If you've brought me a letter, then
just leave it in the mailbox.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.830
Ms. Tanaka!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:46.700
So...

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:50.760
...how old is the woman we'll
be dropping in on?

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:54.350
Let's see... Ms. Ume
Suzuki, wasn't it?

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:56.640
According to
this... Huh?

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.350
What's wrong?

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.480
I've brought the
wrong file.

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:11.750
"Suzuki"

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.270
Bingo! I've hit
the jackpot!

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.270
"Sakurai Bank - Passbook"

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.240
I better not forget
her seal.

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:29.250
Without that, these bank
books are useless.

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:31.370
Now where would
she keep it?

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:42.960
Okay. Well... I'll just
go and get her file.

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:44.630
Sorry about that.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:47.430
Sorry about that.
We all make mistakes. It's no big deal.

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:51.890
I'll take care of the lady
until you get back.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:55.210
That's not too comforting.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:56.310
Why's that?

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:58.500
She's an older woman, you know.
Why's that?

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:02.000
I know! And I can certainly
take care of her.

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:04.820
Just take it easy.

00:08:04.820 --> 00:08:05.650
"Take it easy?"

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.620
Yeah. See you soon.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:11.010
What'd she mean
by that?

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:16.030
I hope she'll
be all right.

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:25.070
Damn! Can't find that seal! Where'd
the old bag hide it?! Geez!

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:27.400
Oh, no! She's
back already!

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.910
No, wait. She wouldn't be
ringing her own doorbell.

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:45.250
The cops! Why?!

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.360
That's weird.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.760
Why wouldn't she be
home at this hour?

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:56.200
Don't tell me that thief
#704 has been here!

00:08:57.840 --> 00:08:59.460
Excuse me! Ms.
Suzuki?

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:01.270
Are you there?

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:04.610
Ms. Suzuki! Are you
home? Hello?

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:07.750
She'll leave soon, once she
realizes nobody's home.

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:13.280
You're in trouble, aren't you?! I'm
gonna break down the door!

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:24.250
Yes? Who is it?

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:28.360
Oh... Ms. Suzuki! You're
home after all!

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.190
Sorry I didn't answer
right away.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:33.000
I was just lying
down.

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:35.200
That's all right. I'm just
glad you're okay.

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:37.270
What do you
mean, dear?

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:40.770
My name's Tsujimoto and
I'm from Bokuto Station...

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:44.650
I just came down here today to see
if you were all right, Ms. Suzuki.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:48.920
Well now, isn't that
the kindest thing?

00:09:49.090 --> 00:09:52.060
<i>I've got to get</i>
<i>rid of her!</i>

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.850
It was very nice of you
to stop by, dear...

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:58.660
...but I'm afraid I've got
a dreadful cold.

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:00.990
Oh? That's
terrible!

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:04.160
Don't worry, ma'am! I'm here now,
and everything will be just fine!

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.740
Now just open up
the door for me.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:06.960
What?!

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.900
"What?" Is something
wrong, ma'am?

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.130
No, not at all.

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:16.140
You just sit tight, while I put myself
together. I'll be right with you.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:26.720
I know everything there is to know
about the old lady who lives here.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:33.020
Nobody's ever been
able to identify me.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:49.880
Here I go!

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:58.550
Hello? Ms. Suzuki?
Are you there?

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:01.250
Are you all right?
Ms. Su...

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:04.160
Yes, dear, I'm here. Sorry
to keep you waiting.

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:08.520
You must have been
so lonely and all.

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:10.690
But rest assured, I'm here
to help you now.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:14.030
Just let me know if there's
anything I can do for you.

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:18.630
Well that's awfully thoughtful of you
dear, but it's just a simple cold...

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:20.510
...nothing to really
worry about.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:23.240
No, ma'am, colds must
be taken seriously!

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:25.510
You just sit back and
rest, Ms. Suzuki.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.350
<i>Oh, boy!</i>

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:32.080
Ms. Suzuki, you really
should lie down.

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:35.250
I'm fine, dear.
Honestly.

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:39.900
You have to make sure to drink lots and
lots of fluids when you have a cold.

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.130
Here you are, ma'am.
Have some tea.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:45.670
Thanks, love.

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:48.370
My goodness, that's hot.

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:56.270
Yuck, maybe it's
a bit too strong.

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:59.420
No, dear, it's just
scrumptious.

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:03.450
<i>I've got to ditch her quickly,</i>
<i>before this gets messy!</i>

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:07.750
Well, look at the time. I suppose
I'd better start making dinner.

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:10.220
Isn't it a little early?

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:11.450
Why, no!

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:15.500
When you get to be my age, love,
everything takes a little longer.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:18.540
Well, I'd better
get started.

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:19.870
Ms. Suzuki!

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:20.530
Huh?

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:23.910
I'll make dinner
for you today!

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:30.410
She's old, so I guess I'd better
go with something traditional.

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:31.340
But...

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.980
...that style's
the hardest!

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:38.160
<i>I don't believe this. I'll have to let her</i>
<i>cook, then brush her off after we eat.</i>

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:44.920
Ms. Tanaka...

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:47.620
If you're ever in trouble, you make sure
to call down to the station, all right?

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:50.100
I'll be down here
in no time at all.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:51.430
You will?

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:52.630
Of course!

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:55.730
I'll come and help
you any time.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:56.810
You can count on me!

00:12:57.240 --> 00:12:58.940
You'll help me?

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:01.810
Well in that case, maybe there
is something you can do.

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:03.440
What is it?

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:05.850
I'd like to return
something...

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:08.540
...I borrowed from my
best friend.

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:10.520
Would you take
it for me?

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:12.150
No problem at all.

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:15.590
Thanks, and sorry
for the bother.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.290
I'll take advantage of
your kindness then.

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:19.290
I'm at your
service.

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:30.240
You actually borrowed a
chest from your friend?

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:32.880
I sure did.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:34.740
I don't know
about this...

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:44.020
Uh-oh. This isn't looking
too good.

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:46.260
Oh, no!

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:47.880
Yow! That's hot!

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:49.930
Oww!

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:51.990
Sorry! Are you
all right?!

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:54.390
It's nothing.
I'm fine.

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:58.370
<i>Ow! How long's it going to take</i>
<i>this broad to make dinner?!</i>

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:01.640
I'm so sorry,
Ms. Suzuki!

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:05.230
Hurry up, Miyuki!
I'm sinking fast!

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:08.300
Miyuki's here!
At last!

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:11.810
<i>Miyuki? Who's she?</i>

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:16.110
Ms. Ume Suzuki.

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:19.680
She's lived alone since her husband
passed away, two years ago.

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:23.230
But her daughter lives
in the neighborhood.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:29.220
Hmm... Isn't she usually at her daughter's
house this time of day?

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:31.060
I'm so glad you
made it!

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:32.970
What's wrong
with you?

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:37.070
Natsumi's been
cooking?

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:41.510
Yes, dear. She's gone out of
her way just for little old me.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.410
But I'll take care of
the rest, now.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:44.570
No, ma'am.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:45.370
Huh?

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:47.980
You just leave dinner
up to me.

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:52.550
All right, let's
get to it.

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:53.450
Okay!

00:14:54.130 --> 00:14:58.530
<i>Damn. All I need is the old lady's</i>
<i>seal, and I can get outta here!</i>

00:14:58.830 --> 00:14:59.520
Ms. Suzuki...

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:00.970
"Nori;" Seaweed
...do you have
any nori?

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:02.130
Yes, love.

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:04.720
Now where did
I put it?

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:07.460
I could have sworn
it was in here.

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:09.340
Hmm? Not there?

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:13.100
That's strange.

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:16.340
Maybe it's in
here. Nope.

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:18.810
<i>She sure is agile.</i>

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:21.280
<i>It's hard to believe</i>
<i>she's 80.</i>

00:15:21.390 --> 00:15:25.320
<i>And how come she doesn't even know</i>
<i>where she keeps her nori?</i>

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:27.190
That reminds me.

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:28.820
We were lucky to find
you home today.

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:29.720
Pardon?

00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:33.830
You're usually at your daughter's
house at this time of day, right?

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:37.130
Yes, but uh, well...
Ow! Ow!

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:41.570
She's got a
cold today.

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:46.040
That's right. And I wouldn't want to give
a cold to my grandchild, now would I?

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:47.840
Here it is! I've
found it.

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:50.740
<i>Something</i>
<i>isn't right.</i>

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:53.840
<i>Why wouldn't her daughter</i>
<i>come to look after her?</i>

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:57.050
Thank you.

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:59.350
<i>There's something</i>
<i>fishy going on.</i>

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:02.120
Huh?

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:05.120
There's a seal
in here.

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:06.990
So that's where
it was!

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:10.500
Your voice sounded
weird.

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:13.800
Oh, yes, my poor
throat.

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:18.330
Huh? Nakajima?!

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:19.810
Tsujimoto?!

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:21.970
Is Ume home?

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:26.740
It's been a
long time.

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:27.520
Huh?

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:29.710
Here.

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:33.320
Here, look. I borrowed this from
you, and I'm bringing it back.

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:37.420
You didn't have
to do that, dear.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:40.360
This young fella packed it all
the way over here for me.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:43.060
He's such a nice,
kind mailman.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.570
I told you, ma'am,
I'm not a...

00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:48.330
Dinner's almost
ready.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:51.570
How about we all
eat together?

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:54.240
Kobayakawa!

00:16:54.350 --> 00:16:55.570
What's with
that apron?

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:58.980
Natsumi and I have been
making dinner.

00:16:59.150 --> 00:17:02.310
Look at you, Nakajima. Don't
you look happy?

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:05.090
Don't be stupid.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:12.290
Ume!

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:13.420
Ume! Are you
listening?

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:14.290
Huh?

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:17.230
Where's that cat of yours that
always sits right here?

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:19.060
Eh?

00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:23.200
Uh... the cat! The
cat's outside.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:28.140
Oh my! The cat's outside
all by itself?

00:17:28.510 --> 00:17:31.240
You know cats. They're
so independent.

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:33.670
What kind of cat is
it, Ms. Suzuki?

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:37.250
What kind? Oh, just
the ordinary kind.

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.310
What color is it?

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:40.850
What color?

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:43.690
It's difficult to pin down
the color, really.

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:45.630
It's uh... well, everyone sees things
a little differently, after all.

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:47.160
Isn't it white?

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:49.400
That's it! It could
be white.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:52.600
What's the cat's name?

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:55.330
N... Name? Its name...

00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:58.580
Did that cat have
a name?

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:00.730
No! I haven't
named it yet!

00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:02.680
That's strange...

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:04.300
...not giving your
cat a name.

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:06.420
Nope. It doesn't
have a name.

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:10.110
That's right. No name.
No name at all.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.960
Of course. Why
would it?

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:14.490
"Why would it?"

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:16.130
Huh?

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:18.290
It's one of those ceramic
"inviting cats."

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:22.720
Can ceramic cats walk?

00:18:22.900 --> 00:18:24.930
Not that I know of.

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:28.170
That's right! Now
I remember!

00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:32.100
I borrowed that
cat from you...

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:33.870
...it was so cute
and lovely.

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:36.410
And that's what I wanted to
bring back to you today.

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:40.180
"10,000,000 ryo (ancient Japanese coin)"

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:42.820
Then what about
the chest?!

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:46.050
The chest belongs
to me.

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:49.150
Sorry, Mr. Mailman, but could you
carry it back home for me?

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:53.330
That must mean...

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:54.970
It does mean...

00:18:57.670 --> 00:18:58.640
Umm...

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:01.570
You're a phony
granny!

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:07.670
Oh my goodness.

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:11.310
I've been cloned!

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:15.610
You tricked us!

00:19:16.350 --> 00:19:17.550
You impostor!

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:29.770
Come clean, now!

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:32.290
Stand up, man!

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:34.390
You're wrong! You've
got it all wrong!

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:36.570
She's the impostor!

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:44.140
This cat can tell who
the real granny is.

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:46.480
The cat never lies!

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:49.220
I'm sorry.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:58.730
Imagine that! A man
disguised as you!

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:01.590
I'm so glad you weren't
hurt, Sayuri.

00:20:02.030 --> 00:20:05.090
Well, Ms. Tanaka? Shall
we be on our way?

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:08.830
Yes, thank you so much,
Mr. Mailman.

00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:32.830
Are you sure about this? You really
didn't have to come, you know.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:34.060
It's okay.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:37.600
Natsumi can drive the car back
now that she has a license.

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:42.570
Something the matter,
Ms. Tanaka?

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:44.700
I wonder how many...

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:49.210
...old folks like me there are in this
town, living all by themselves.

00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:50.840
Hmm?

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:03.490
Say, are you two
married?

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:06.020
No, nothing like
that, ma'am.

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:10.600
Is that so? I'm not usually
wrong about such things.

00:21:10.940 --> 00:21:12.770
Now if I'd had
children...

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:15.770
...I suppose my grandchildren
would be about your age.

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:18.900
She doesn't have
any children.

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:20.130
Oh, I see.

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:24.710
I think today turned out
to be a lovely day.

00:21:24.980 --> 00:21:26.180
You do?

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:31.790
Yes. Meeting people like you makes
me glad I've lived as long as I have.

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:33.680
Well, Ms. Tanaka...

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:35.990
I hope you have many years
ahead of you, too.

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:39.690
That's kind of you to
say. Thank you.

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:45.060
You've got lots of things
to keep living for.

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:46.900
I suppose I do.

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:49.040
Of course you do!

00:21:55.450 --> 00:22:00.950
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:11.560
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:18.460
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:28.580
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:28.650 --> 00:22:42.550
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:42.890 --> 00:22:50.730
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:58.610
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:07.450
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:17.020
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:24.500
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:27.770
"Declaration of War"

00:23:28.370 --> 00:23:31.000
Peace is good and
tea is good, too.

00:23:31.110 --> 00:23:32.670
What the heck are you
talking about?

00:23:32.780 --> 00:23:36.040
Yeah! Nakajima, it's because you're
like that that Miyuki is... Miyuki is...

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:37.480
What happened to
Kobayakawa?

00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:40.180
Well, this cool biker
dude showed up...

00:23:40.420 --> 00:23:41.650
Who the hell is he?

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:43.480
A relative of
your mom.

00:23:43.590 --> 00:23:44.250
Huh?!

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:46.560
Next time, You're Under Arrest, File 29...

00:23:46.620 --> 00:23:48.430
..."A Rival Appears; A Heated Race."

00:23:48.490 --> 00:23:51.330
If you're a man,
then show us!
